      "text": " Let us learn about number of moons orbiting each of the eight planets in our solar system."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:20.654",
      "start": "00:00:15.315",
      "text": " Mercury, the closest planet to the Sun, does not have any moons."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:25.158",
      "start": "00:00:20.654",
      "text": " Similar to Mercury, Venus also does not have any moons."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:28.862",
      "start": "00:00:25.158",
      "text": " Earth has one natural satellite, simply called the Moon."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:35.669",
      "start": "00:00:28.862",
      "text": " It plays a significant role in Earth's tides and has been explored extensively by humans."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:39.540",
      "start": "00:00:35.669",
      "text": " Mars has two small moons named Phobos and Dimos."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:44.144",
